Description: GHSA-3mg3-cr28-46gc (CVE-2026-129292, the PHP security release of 19.11.2026): FPM XSS within status endpoint via user and script; the fix of this branch (00922d4f01) escapes the request method, the URI, the query string, the user and the script for the HTML and XML pages only; for 7.4 these five fields escaped for the JSON page too, by an escaper of its own that writes them as php_json_encode_string() of 8.x does with PHP_JSON_INVALID_UTF8_IGNORE (the json of 7.4 can be a module of its own, which FPM cannot call; 20.11.2026); its tests not taken
Origin: php-src commit 1ecb92f2cdeb235bb10d6c220c9be4a13f527243 (Jakub Zelenka, 26.10.2026, PHP 8.2.36): its escaping of the JSON page

diff --git a/sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_status.c b/sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_status.c
index e966d94561..df8ee135e5 100644
--- a/sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_status.c
+++ b/sapi/fpm/fpm/fpm_status.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include "fpm_conf.h"
 #include "fpm_php.h"
 #include <ext/standard/html.h>
